# Two independent concerns, both load-bearing.
#
# 1. Never send local credentials or private key material to a Docker builder.
#    The runtime images receive secrets only when the platform starts them.
#
# 2. Keep the build context small: docker/docker-compose*.yml build the
#    service images with the repo root as context (Dockerfiles COPY
#    repo-root-relative paths), so without this file every local build ships
#    multi-GB build artifacts to the daemon. CI checkouts are clean, which is
#    why this was never noticed there.

# --- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/kubeconfig
**/kubeconfig.*
**/*.kubeconfig
**/.npmrc
**/.netrc
**/id_rsa
**/id_ed25519

# --- build context size ------------------------------------------------------
target
**/node_modules
**/dist
explorer/.astro
sdk/typescript/coverage
sdk/react/coverage
.planning
